      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_164"
      ],
      "explanation": "An exponent of \\(-1\\) means the reciprocal of a nonzero number. First,\n\\[\n2-3=-1,\n\\qquad (2-3)^{-1}=\\frac1{-1}=-1.\n\\]\nTherefore\n\\[\n\\left[2-3(2-3)^{-1}\\right]^{-1}\n=\\left[2-3(-1)\\right]^{-1}\n=5^{-1}\n=\\frac15.\n\\]\nBoth reciprocal bases, \\(-1\\) and \\(5\\), are nonzero. The answer is \\(\\frac15\\), choice C.",
